Calc keeps Excel's dynamic arrays through XLSX

Excel marks a spilling array formula with cm="1" on its anchor cell,
pointing into xl/metadata.xml (an XLDAPR block, fDynamic="1"). Calc
read neither and wrote neither, so a saved workbook turned SORT(),
FILTER() and the like into fixed legacy arrays that no longer spill
(Ely R15.11a). Import reads metadata.xml and flags the array origins
whose cm names a dynamic block; the flag follows the cell through
copies; export writes cm="1" on flagged origins and the metadata part
with its relationship.
